  "description": "Learn Flow States in one minute.",
  "is_free": false,
  "published": true,
  "story": {
    "hook": {
      "text": "A basketball player sinks seven three-pointers in a row and later says time slowed down, the crowd vanished, and the basket.",
      "visual": "🏀"
    },
    "buildup": {
      "text": "Flow is a state of complete absorption in an activity where self-consciousness disappears and performance peaks.",
      "visual": "🌊"
    },
    "discovery": {
      "text": "During flow, the prefrontal cortex partially deactivates, a process called transient hypofrontality. The inner critic goes quiet.",
      "visual": "🤫"
    },
    "twist": {
      "text": "Flow also shifts brainwaves from beta to the borderline between alpha and theta, a zone associated with creativity and relaxed.",
      "visual": "〰️"
    },
    "climax": {
      "text": "Studies suggest people in flow are up to 500 percent more productive and report the highest levels of satisfaction in their lives.",
      "visual": "📈"
    },
    "punchline": {
      "text": "Flow is not thinking harder.",
      "visual": "🎯"
    }
  },
  "quiz": {
    "question": "What happens to the prefrontal cortex during flow?",
    "options": [
      "It partially deactivates, silencing the inner critic",
      "It becomes maximally active to boost performance",
      "It switches to processing visual information"
    ],
    "correct": 0
  },
